{% if part == "LyricsWikifonia" %}\lyricmode {
	Lit -- tle Wil -- ly Green from New Or -- leans, a greed -- y boy was he.
	He al -- ways want -- ed lots of kids just to keep him com -- pan -- y.
	One day his Mom bought him a Toot -- sie roll, the best can -- dy that was made.
	When the kids be -- gan to hang a -- round, lit -- tle Wil -- ly said: I ain't gon -- na give no -- bod -- y none of my Toot -- sie Roll,
	(Toot -- sie Roll) I would -- n't give you a piece of my sweet,
	not to save your soul! (save your soul!) Dad -- dy told me to -- day,
	Just be -- fore he went a -- way, If I'd be a good boy,
	He'd bring me a toy; And I'm my Dad -- dy's pride and joy!
	You know there ain't no need in your just hang -- in' a -- round,
	(hang -- in' a -- round) I know you want it, but I'm a gon -- na turn you down.
	My Toot -- sie Roll is sweet! _ _ And you know it can't be beat!
	_ _ I know you want it, but you can't have it! I ain't a gon -- na give you none!
}
{% endif %}
